[174.64, "o", "\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[1A\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⏺\u001b[0m \u001b[1mRan 2 shell commands\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[90m  ⎿  Bash(cd /tmp && ls node_modules/jsdom >/dev/null 2>&1 || npm i jsdom --silent 2>&1 | tail -1; node -e…\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[183.545, "o", "\r\n\u001b[97m⏺ I've extended `prototype.html` (same file, same way of opening it). A scripted smoke test in jsdom, a\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  simulated browser with no real layout, ran every screen and the record, finish and save flow without errors.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  I haven't looked at it in a real browser, so layout and the animations are unchecked.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  **What's new**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Onboarding:** after sign-in there are three steps. You pick road or gravel, set a weekly distance goal\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  (which renames and resizes your weekly challenge), then follow suggested riders and grant location access.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Notifications:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - The Feed has a 🔔 with an unread count.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - The inbox covers streak at risk, segment beaten and challenge progress. Tapping an item jumps to the\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  relevant screen.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - There are working push-setting toggles.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Saving a ride later triggers live toasts: kudos from Maya after about 5 seconds, and a segment rank-up\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  after about 12.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Social:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Tap any avatar for a rider profile with a Follow/Unfollow button. Unfollowing removes that rider's rides\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  from your feed.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - A Suggested riders section appears in the feed.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Segments:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - The Feed now has Rides and Segments tabs, with your rank on each segment.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - You can create a segment from the feed, or from a ride summary after you finish.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - The friends, club and local leaderboards now show different results.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Recording:**\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - The Road/Gravel toggle now works and is saved on the ride.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - A dot moves along the route while you ride.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m    - Segment-ahead and segment-started alerts appear mid-ride.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Gamification:** XP now carries over into real levels. Level-ups get confetti and an XP bar animation,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  and each saved ride unlocks the next locked badge. Challenge progress goes up from your ride's distance,\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  climb and ride count.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Pro:** the stats card is now a real chart of weekly distance with a fitness trend line. It's blurred\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  until you unlock Pro.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  - **Labs tab (v2 preview):** a hex territory map on your Profile. Tap hexes to claim neutral ones or capture\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  rival ones for XP. It also lists the other v2 features.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  \u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  If you meant something else by \"further\", say which direction. Options include a real map using Leaflet\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[97m  tiles, light mode, a Pro-only club admin dashboard, or a guided demo that walks through the main flow.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
